.TH WEZTERM-SWITCH-TAB 1 "2026-07-04" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wezterm-switch-tab \- request a WezTerm or parent tmux tab switch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wezterm-switch-tab
.RI [ next | previous ]
.RI [ tty ]
.br
.B wezterm-switch-tab
.RI [ next | previous ]
.B --tty
.I tty
.br
.B wezterm-switch-tab
.B --parent
.RI [ next | previous ]
.RI [ tty ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wezterm-switch-tab
emits a WezTerm OSC 1337
.B SetUserVar
request for tab switching. Consumers such as tmux can bind keys to this helper
when the focused application cannot handle the key itself.
.PP
Normal requests set
.B DOT_SWITCH_TAB
and are handled by the outer WezTerm process. Parent requests set
.B DOT_PARENT_SWITCH_TAB
inside tmux DCS passthrough framing so the request can escape an inner tmux and
be translated by WezTerm into the parent tmux layer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --tty \fItty\fR
Write the request to
.I tty
instead of
.B $WEZTERM_SWITCH_TAB_TTY
or
.B /dev/tty .
.TP
.B --parent
Bubble the switch request to the parent tmux layer.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B next
Switch to the next tab or tmux window. This is the default.
.TP
.B previous
Switch to the previous tab or tmux window.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wezterm-switch-tab next /dev/ttys001
wezterm-switch-tab previous --tty /dev/ttys001
wezterm-switch-tab --parent next /dev/ttys001
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The request was written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wezterm-move-tab (1)
